From 0f69201998ec7e364a8307ae157ee8fa0ab99c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:57:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): a @session ref opens on the gateway that owns
 the session [daveey]

Clicking @session:default/<id> opened the bare id against the ACTIVE gateway.
With a cloud gateway selected, a local session's tab probed only the cloud
backend, found nothing and stayed blank.

openSessionRef now resolves the owner first (gateway qualifier -> unified-list
row tag, or the registry primary for an untagged row -> owner hint -> the
gateway of the chat showing the link) and openSession pins that route on the
new tile. The SessionView context moves to a store-free module so transcript
chips can read their enclosing chat without pulling the session store graph.
